# Set the held object down. Target — give EXACTLY ONE of the first two
# pairs, or neither:
#   1. (x, y) metres in the arm base frame — carry the object there and set
#      it down;
#   2. (u, v) pixel in the camera's RGB image (1280x720, as delivered by the
#      camera primitive, i.e. the RAW/uncorrected frame a client displays) —
#      the skill undistorts it with camera_matrix/dist_coeffs, then maps it
#      through the 2D hand-eye homography_matrix to base XY;
#   3. with neither pair given: the configured `place_pose` when calibrated;
#   4. otherwise IN PLACE (原地放下) — the arm's current XY.
# Passing a metres pair AND a pixel pair is an error (ambiguous target).
# z is always the configured desktop_height and the orientation grasp_rpy,
# so the target only moves in the table plane. Either way: hover above the
# target (z + travel_offset), descend, open the gripper, settle, lift back
# to hover. The mirror of grab — the gripper keeps holding until the
# bottom, unlike release which lets go where the arm is.
#
# The framework has no optional MCP arguments — every field is required in
# the tool schema — so "not given" is spelled 0/0: x = 0 AND y = 0 means no
# metres target, u = 0 AND v = 0 means no pixel target; all four 0 means no
# target at all. (0, 0) is the base column in metres and the top-left corner
# in pixels — neither is a reachable place point on this arm.
float64 x
float64 y
float64 u
float64 v
---
# Whether the flow completed (every waypoint converged or a non-fatal
# lift failure was reported in `message`).
bool success

# Human-readable status. On failure, names the failing stage
# (preflight / geometry / place/approach / place/descend / place/open /
# place/lift).
string message

# How long the whole call took (s).
float32 elapsed_s
